              Digital Sets New Performance Standard for
         Value Notebooks with Introduction of HiNote VP 500


  Enterprise-Ready Clients Ideal for Mobile Computing Professionals


MAYNARD, Mass., September 30, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today solidified its leadership position in the enterprise mobile 
computing market with its newest value-priced notebook computer 
family, the Digital HiNote VP 500.  With entry-level prices starting 
at approximately U.S. $2,499 (estimated street price), the new 
series is an aggressively priced line of 120- or 133-megahertz (MHz) 
Pentium-based notebooks that combines high-level performance and 
system modularity, while at the same time offering unique 
connectivity and manageability features to better meet the needs 
of enterprise customers.

     "With the introduction of the new HiNote VP 500, Digital is 
taking the next step in bringing high-level performance and 
functionality into the value segment of the mobile computing 
market," said Howard Elias, vice president of worldwide business 
segments in Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit. "Today's 
announcement reinforces once again our leadership in mobile client 
computing, building on the success of the HiNote Ultra II product 
line."

High-Level Performance in a Value-Line Notebook

     The HiNote VP 500 modular notebook series maintains Digital's 
edge in providing industry-leading performance and high-end features 
at aggressive prices.  The systems have been optimized to deliver 
maximum performance and raise the bar for value leadership in mobile 
computing to new heights.  

     Industry-standard benchmark tests measuring overall system 
performance demonstrate the HiNote VP 500s superior value and 
performance against other leading notebook competitors including 
Compaq, Toshiba and IBM.  For example, the 133MHz HiNote VP 535 
model performed more than 40 percent faster overall than Compaq's 
LTE 5300 or Toshiba's Tecra 720CDT, and 16 percent faster than IBM's 
high-end ThinkPad 760ED model -- at half the cost of the IBM system.

     The HiNote VP 500 -- which joins Digital's award-winning HiNote 
Ultra II family of thin, lightweight ultraportable notebooks -- 
offers leading-edge mobile multimedia features such as 12.1- and 
11.3-inch SVGA (Super Video Graphics Array) dual-scan or active-
matrix color displays; a 128-bit graphics accelerator with MPEG 
(Motion Pictures Expert Group) support for rich, full-motion video 
playback, and a removable, internal 6X-speed CD-ROM drive in the 
system's modular expansion bay.

     The HiNote VP 500 series also delivers longer battery life 
through the use of leading-edge battery technologies.  An "Advanced 
Metal" Smart Battery using Enhanced NiMH (Nickel Metal Hydride) 
technology comes standard with each system.  A second, dual-battery 
option using Smart Lithium-Ion (LiIon) technology can be placed in the 
system's modular expansion bay, delivering a full workday's run-time of 
up to 10 hours. "Smart" battery technology incorporates intelligent 
electronics within the battery casing, which provides support for external 
indicators on the battery to show the charge level and allows the 
system to manage charging and discharging of the battery to extend 
the overall lifetime of the battery itself.

Modular Design Supports Flexible System Expansion

     The HiNote VP 500 series features a modular, expandable design 
that provides mobile professionals with the flexibility to customize 
the notebook to best match their individual needs.  Each system has 
a modular expansion bay for support of the notebook's removable 
floppy drive, that is interchangeable with the CD-ROM drive or an 
optional Smart LiIon second battery.  The expandable line of HiNote 
VP 500 notebooks scales from 8-megabytes (MB) of Extended Data Out 
(EDO) system memory up to 40MB, using optional 8, 16 and 32MB EDO 
memory upgrade modules.  In addition, the system includes removable 
hard drives that support up to 1.08- or 1.44-gigabytes of storage 
capacity.

"Get Connected" to the Enterprise

     The Digital HiNote VP 500 series is the ideal choice for mobile 
professionals who need the most performance for the money in 
enterprise-ready mobile client solutions.  The new line of 
network-ready HiNote VP 500 notebooks are designed to keep mobile 
users connected with pre-loaded Digital ClientWORKS network 
management software, DMI support and expansion options that include 
a port replicator with built-in network connectivity.

     The HiNote VP 500 series comes pre-loaded with Windows 95 or 
Windows for Workgroups 3.11 and is fully Windows NT-certified.  
Reinforcing Digital's leadership in bringing Windows NT-based 
computing across the enterprise and into the mobile environment, the 
company will offer a Windows NT 4.0 driver kit for the HiNote VP 500 
notebooks next quarter.

Pricing and Availability

     The HiNote VP 500 family is targeted at mobile professionals in 
small- to large-sized businesses who need connectivity to the 
enterprise anytime, anywhere.  The new models are available 
immediately through Digital's channel partners, including authorized 
resellers and select retail outlets.   Estimated street prices range 
from U.S. $2,499 to $3,699.  A broad range of optional system 
accessories and upgrade kits are available, including the Smart 
LiIon second battery for $279 and the port replicator with 
integrated Ethernet networking for $319.

     Digital's solutions are the leading choice for customers 
deploying Windows-based computing across the enterprise.  The 
company offers enterprise customers superior value with client/
server solutions optimized for Windows and Windows NT environments, 
global services and support, and solutions delivered through 
alliances with industry leaders.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scaleable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
