                    Digital Equipment Corporation
     Declares Regular Cash Dividend on Series A Preferred Stock


On September 26, 1996 the Board of Directors of Digital Equipment 
Corporation (NYSE::DEC) declared a regular cash dividend on its 
Series A 8 7/8% Cumulative Preferred Stock for the period from July 
16 through October 15, 1996.  The dividend is equivalent to $.555 
per depositary share.  Each depositary share represents ownership of 
one-fourth of a share of Series A 8 7/8% Cumulative Preferred Stock, 
par value $1.00 per share, issued March 21, 1994.

     Dividends are payable on October 15, 1996 to stockholders of 
record at the close of business on October 1, 1996.  The dividend 
payment for the period totals $8,875,000 for four million shares of 
Preferred Stock outstanding.

