                Digital Opens AltaVista ForumForum --
              Community Collaboration Moves Onsite with
           the First Virsual Office Tower on the Internet

MAYNARD, Mass., September 27, 1996 -- In a unique demonstration of 
the power of collaboration on the Internet, Digital Equipment 
Corporation today unveiled AltaVista ForumForum.  AltaVista 
ForumForum is a WorldWide Web-based technology showcase for the 
sharing of ideas, opinions, and business information and to bring 
together communities of Internet users with shared interests.

     AltaVista ForumForum, located at http://altavista.forum.
digital.com, will host a thousand different communities, each 
provided with an unprecedented set of Internet messaging, polling 
and document sharing capabilities.  Like AltaVista Search Public 
Service, AltaVista ForumForum is a free service and a powerful 
demonstration of AltaVista's OnSite Computing vision, bringing the 
vast potential of the Internet to productive work and creative 
expression at any place, at any time.

     Among the communities housed on 'floors' in the Internet's 
first 'virtual office tower' will be those devoted to charities, 
professional societies and technical service.  Out of the 1,000 
floors available on AltaVista ForumForum, 700 already house 
'tenants'' who begin moving in today. Applications are being 
accepted for the remaining 300 floors.

     "With AltaVista ForumForum, we plan to capture the same magic 
as we created with AltaVista Search, the most popular search service 
on the WorldWide Web," said Ilene H. Lang, vice president of 
Digital's Internet Software Business Unit.  "The immense potential 
of the Internet is finally becoming realized, and AltaVista 
ForumForum is a bold step forward in the development of virtual 
communities."

     The AltaVista ForumForum public service is a combination of 
public and private communities.  Using such capabilities as 
post-and-reply discussion, email, password security, document 
sharing and opinion polling, each floor's moderator develops the 
community concept, establishes membership criteria and maintains 
areas for discussion forums and document sharing. On public floors, 
any Internet user with a Web browser can participate.  On the 
private floors, moderators set guidelines on membership.

     After entering ForumForum, visitors enter the main lobby where 
they sign in, join a guided tour of the facility or access the 
building directory. The Lobby also contains a help desk and a 
registration area which processes new guests.  Using a virtual 
elevator to reach their selected floor, visitors can join teams to 
participate in group discussions, surveys, and share documents and 
other down loadable software including Java applets. Based on the 
AltaVista Forum V2.0 product, ForumForum also provides collaboration 
centers complete with general team information, calendars and 
calling cards; and sophisticated news filtering to deliver data of 
interest to the team.  AltaVista Forum technology also supports IRC 
text chatting.

     Leasing terms for tenants of this virtual office tower include 
a free 30 day lease with an option for a 30-day extension.  After 
the end of the lease, floor moderators can, with the purchase of 
AltaVista Forum V2.0, or with the purchase of AltaVista ForumForum 
hosting services offered by AltaVista Business Partners, move their 
community with a link from their AltaVista ForumForum floor to their 
server or service.

     AltaVista OnSite Computing solutions provide high performance 
Internet connectivity to help cyberworkers quickly find useful 
information, easily communicate and collaborate over secure virtual 
networks.  Further information is available at http://altavista.
software.digital.com.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
sever solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scalable Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete  
and win in today's global marketplace.
