                  Digital and Microsoft Demonstrate
     Windows NT Solutions for AS/400 Environments At COMMON '96

                            COMMON '96 
                            Booth #748

ATLANTA, GA -- October 20, 1996 --  Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Microsoft Corporation demonstrated Windows NT solutions at 
COMMON '96 that enhance and protect customers' investments in IBM 
AS/400 systems and business applications. COMMON '96 is the largest 
IBM user conference and exposition, which opened here today at the 
Atlanta Hilton and Towers. 

     At the show, Digital and Microsoft demonstrated how AS/400 
users can offload their systems to serve business applications more 
efficiently.

     "Windows NT offers AS/400 users a taste of newer, more powerful 
solutions for personal productivity," said David Booth, director of 
Digital's AlphaServer Reseller Initiative.  "Microsoft and Digital 
deliver the best method for integrating PCs into AS/400 environments 
as well as fast, low-cost data warehousing solutions."

     "AS/400 managers are deploying Windows NT Servers in increasing 
numbers to implement file, print, web, and database connectivity 
solutions for their users," said Vesa Suomalainen, general manager 
of the host integration product unit at Microsoft. "The strategy 
behind SNA Server is to tightly integrate the Windows NT Server 
environment with the AS/400, while providing easy, efficient, and 
cost-effective AS/400 connectivity for desktop users."

PC Connectivity with Microsoft SNA Server

     Some 400,000 AS/400 systems hold the business-critical data of 
organizations. Microsoft's SNA Server enables AS/400 users to 
connect IBM hosts to PCs flexibly, securely, and economically. By 
implementing Microsoft SNA Server on Digital's Windows NT platforms, 
users get improved host performance, easy administration of host 
connections, an extra layer of security, among other benefits.

     Other Microsoft components necessary for AS/400 integration 
include: Microsoft BackOffice, the server software;  Microsoft 
Office, the client software; Microsoft Windows NT Server, a 
client/server network operating system; Microsoft SQL Server, a 
high-performance relational database management system; Microsoft 
Exchange, which provides a basic infrastructure for electronic mail; 
and Microsoft Systems Management Server, the fundamental instrument 
for managing PCs in a LAN environment.

     "Much of the mission-critical data that PC users need resides 
on systems such as the AS/400.  Microsoft's products can tightly 
integrate PCs and LANs with AS/400 systems, giving users access to 
the data they need to make better decisions," says Booth. "Digital's 
AlphaServer systems running Microsoft SNA Server software can 
support thousands of users and still have power left to run other 
server applications."

Low-Cost Data Warehousing Solution

     Data warehousing, once known only in the shops of large retail 
and manufacturing concerns, is now migrating to mid-sized companies 
and even departments within companies. Typically, many AS/400 sites 
are already overloaded with business applications, providing few 
options for building data warehouses. 

     Digital, Microsoft, Data Mirror, and ExecuSoft Systems offer 
AS/400 users access to a data warehouse that is fast, low-priced, 
and easy to use. Digital provides highly scalable AlphaServer 
systems; Microsoft provides its Windows NT suite of products; and 
ExecuSoft and Data Mirror provide high-speed transfer and data 
replication software. 

     The solution enables users to replicate DB2 data stored on an 
AS/400 to a platform running Microsoft SQL Server software. The DB2 
database remains on the AS/400 system but the Windows NT platform 
processes all data queries. This frees the AS/400 system to perform 
other applications. 

     "This low-cost data warehousing solution gives companies the 
best of both worlds," said Booth. "AS/400 users get a cost-effective 
method by which to add more clients and functionality, plus better 
response times on queries and easier access to existing corporate 
data. Furthermore, offloading these functions from AS/400 systems 
increases the performance of mission-critical applications and 
extends the lifespan of the servers," he added.

Solutions from Partners

     A number of Digital's partners demonstrated their client/server 
solutions for AS/400 environments in the Microsoft/Digital booth. 
These include: the Complementary Products Group, ExecuSoft, Wall 
Data, and Netsoft.  Two of Digital's value-added resellers -- Sun 
Data, Inc. and Systematic Systems Integration -- also showcased 
their software on Digital's Windows NT platforms. 

     Digital offers the widest range of Windows NT servers -- from 
Intel (CISC) to 64-bit AlphaServers systems (RISC) -- and clustering 
for unlimited growth potential.

     Founded in 1975, Microsoft (NASDAQ "MSFT") is the worldwide 
leader in software for personal computers. The company offers a wide 
range of products and services for business and personal use, each 
designed with the mission of making it easier and more enjoyable for 
people to take advantage of the full power of personal computing 
every day.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
