               Digital Expands Fast Ethernet Offering

MAYNARD, Mass., October 28, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today enhanced its network switching line with a product that makes 
it easy for businesses to incorporate high-speed connectivity into 
their workgroup and branch office networks. The EtherWORKS Switch 
8T/TX provides eight ports, each of which automatically "senses" 
whether the attached device is running at Fast Ethernet (100 Mb/s) 
or Ethernet (10Mb/s) speed. This flexibility lets businesses phase 
in the higher speed connections they need to provide users with fast 
access to central servers and corporate backbones and to support 
dedicated desktop connections for high-performance applications such 
as graphics and financial modeling. 

     The EtherWORKS Switch 8T/TX is the newest member of Digital's 
EtherWORKS family of switches and hubs, which brings low-cost, 
high-speed shared and switched networking solutions to workgroups, 
branch offices and small sites. Like the other EtherWORKS products, 
this new switch features desktop packaging that enables customers to 
set up and use their Ethernet local area networks (LANs) in an 
office environment. 

     The EtherWORKS Switch 8T/TX offers several features that 
maximize performance and ensure that businesses have plenty of 
capacity for existing and new users. To deliver top performance,
the switch features cut-through design, full duplex support of up to 
200 Mb/s, a 256K buffer for each port and low packet transmission 
latency (20 microseconds or less). 

     To accommodate both legacy LANs and new users, the switch 
provides industry-standard auto-negotiation, supports over 4,000 MAC 
addresses, provides a routing table of 4,000 entries per port and 
includes an Ethernet address learning function.  It is also fully 
compliant with IEEE 802.3 and IEEE 802.3u standards, ensuring 
interoperability with a full range of networking products. 

     Customers can configure the EtherWORKS Switch 8T/TX as a single 
switch or in combination with other EtherWORKS products.  Other 
members of the EtherWORKS family include:

    o EtherWORKS Switch 8T -- 8-port 10BaseT switch   
    o EtherWORKS Switch 6T/2TX -- 6-port 10BaseT, 2-port 100BaseTX switch  
    o EtherWORKS Switch 2TTX -- 2-port, 10BaseT or 100BaseTX switch   
    o EtherWORKS Hub 8T -- 8-port 10BaseT hub 
    o EtherWORKS Hub 16T -- 16-pot 10BaseT hub   
    o EtherWORKS Hub 8TX -- 8-port 100BaseTX hub 

    Available in November, the EtherWORKS Switch 8T/TX has a U.S. 
List Price of $4,950 ($619 per port). A one-year return-to-Digital 
warranty is included. 

    Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computers to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
